", "legacy_segment_id": 761804, "network_name": "CBS", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "5dbvk9O530", "broadcast_date": "2004-08-09", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 2, "distributor": 9, "broadcast_title": "CBS Evening News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1690, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 761803, "segment_id": "KPQdxX5zse", "segment_broadcast_id": "5dbvk9O530", "segment_title": "Campaign 04 / Bush vs. Kerry / Iraq War", "segment_description": "(Studio: Scott Pelley) Report introduced. \n (Grand Canyon: Jim Axelrod) The policies of Senator John Kerry & President Bush for dealing with Iraq compared; scenes shown of Kerry at the Grand Canyon. [KERRY \u2013 questions why Bush rushed to war without a plan to win the peace.] [BUSH \u2013 defends his decision to go to war.]", "segment_duration": 130, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63200.0", "legacy_segment_id": 761805, "network_name": "CBS", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "5dbvk9O530", "broadcast_date": "2004-08-09", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 2, "distributor": 9, "broadcast_title": "CBS Evening News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1690, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 761803, "segment_id": "7XqF4zEo1p", "segment_broadcast_id": "5dbvk9O530", "segment_title": "Economy: Oil Prices, Stocks", "segment_description": "(Studio: Scott Pelley) Crude oil prices cited; Stock Market Report.", "segment_duration": 10, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63330.0", "legacy_segment_id": 761806, "network_name": "CBS", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "5dbvk9O530", "broadcast_date": "2004-08-09", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 2, "distributor": 9, "broadcast_title": "CBS Evening News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1690, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 761803, "segment_id": "c7bRd1iaAd", "segment_broadcast_id": "5dbvk9O530", "segment_title": "Terrorism / Al Qaeda Threat / Financial Institutions", "segment_description": "(Studio: Scott Pelley) Report introduced. \n (FBI: Jim Stewart) The hunt for Al Qaeda operative Adnan Shukrijumah&#134;, who may have conducted surveillance at financial institution in New York, featured; details given of the evidence pointing to Shukrijumah, including his association with Issa al-Hindi&#134;&#134;, who was captured in Britain last week, and of evidence indicating that Al Qaeda may try to use helicopters as weapons. [May 26, Attorney General John ASHCROFT \u2013 comments on the search for 7 Al Qaeda suspects.] [New York City Mayor Michael BLOOMBERG \u2013 says 9/11 taught you that aircraft can be used as weapons.]", "segment_duration": 140, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63340.0", "legacy_segment_id": 761807, "network_name": "CBS", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "5dbvk9O530", "broadcast_date": "2004-08-09", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 2, "distributor": 9, "broadcast_title": "CBS Evening News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1690, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 761803, "segment_id": "qo1EoWdeij", "segment_broadcast_id": "5dbvk9O530", "segment_title": "Oklahoma City, Oklahoma / Nichols Trial", "segment_description": "(Studio: Scott Pelley) The sentencing of Oklahoma City bomber Terry Nichols on his state conviction reported.", "segment_duration": 30, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63480.0", "legacy_segment_id": 761808, "network_name": "CBS", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "5dbvk9O530", "broadcast_date": "2004-08-09", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 2, "distributor": 9, "broadcast_title": "CBS Evening News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1690, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 761803, "segment_id": "KcXq34hJIa", "segment_broadcast_id": "5dbvk9O530", "segment_title": "Auto Industry / SUV Safety", "segment_description": "(Studio: Scott Pelley) Report introduced.   (New York: Jim Acosta) The new rating system for measuring the risk of SUV rollover featured; rollover test results, including the poor rating for the Ford Explorer, cited. [National Highway Traffic Safety Administration Dr. Jeffrey RUNGE&#134;, \u201cConsumer Reports\u201d R. David PITTLE&#134;- comment on the test results.] [SUV Owners of America Ron DeFORE&#134;- says the largest SUVs and 4-door sedans have the lowest fatality rates.]", "segment_duration": 120, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63510.0", "legacy_segment_id": 761809, "network_name": "CBS", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "5dbvk9O530", "broadcast_date": "2004-08-09", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 2, "distributor": 9, "broadcast_title": "CBS Evening News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1690, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 761803, "segment_id": "NF51K